meson: build the threads compile_args as a conditional list

On hosts without pthread_condattr_setclock() (macOS) the ternary

    has_setclock ? '-DPTHREAD_HAS_SETCLOCK' : ''

yields an empty string, which meson passes to the compiler verbatim as
'', and gcc then fails with "linker input file not found". Build the
argument list conditionally instead, so nothing is passed when a define
is not wanted; hosts that do have pthread_condattr_setclock() keep
PTHREAD_HAS_SETCLOCK.

Replaces the earlier ppcports fix-silly-bug.patch, which simply dropped
the PTHREAD_HAS_SETCLOCK entry. Upstream issue:
https://github.com/haasn/libplacebo/issues/361 (still open).

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index dba8fbff..89d5b94e 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -508,10 +508,17 @@ else
                      args: c_opts,
                    )
 
+    threads_args = []
+    if pthreads.found()
+      threads_args += ['-DPL_HAVE_PTHREAD']
+    endif
+    if has_setclock
+      threads_args += ['-DPTHREAD_HAS_SETCLOCK']
+    endif
+
     threads = declare_dependency(
       dependencies: pthreads,
-      compile_args: [pthreads.found() ? '-DPL_HAVE_PTHREAD' : '',
-                     has_setclock ? '-DPTHREAD_HAS_SETCLOCK' : '',]
+      compile_args: threads_args,
     )
 endif
 
